- develop a psychophysical framework and collected a largescale dataset measuring perception of dichoptic stimuli with 12,989 human subject study trials;
- fit a model over three variables (blur, sharpen, and eccentricity) that predicts quality in just-objectionable-differences (JODs);
- leverage the model as an application to improve foveated rendering, which demonstrates the potential for ~50% compute savings at similar perceptual quality.
